            "rationale": "Continue-coat is refused. Serialized reconstruction: t_um = k_g * (I_sn/I_fe) * (V/V0) = 4.00 * (12.00/4.00) * (800.00/640.00) = 15.00, which is 7.00 um over the 8.00 isolate floor and 65.00 um under the 80.00 hall-kill tripwire, and GD-OES SNR is 12.0 >= 8.0. Intensity-ratio identity I_sn/I_fe = 12.00/4.00 = 3.00; voltage-table identity V/V0 = 800.00/640.00 = 1.25; areal-mass identity m = t * rho = 15.00 * 0.80 = 12.00 g/m2. Lumped k_g without the voltage table under-reads 15.00 as 12.00 and is not SoT. Permit clock was slid 40.00 s and vendor coating packets were dropped, so Plateveil is a collusion party (coating vendor plus operator plus permit clerk Tamsin Brier). Ordered: refuse continue-coat now. Scope: this REJECT does not ESD the tinplate hall (that is the companion question) and does not isolate the Fe internal-standard millivolt.",
            "threshold": "t_um>=8.00 AND gdoes_snr>=8.0 => refuse continue-coat; Plateveil is not SoT; hall-kill if t_um>=80.00; lumped k_g without V/V0 is not SoT",
            "stated_residuals": "line-hold still required to hold the 15.00 um; 15.00 vs a true 80.00 kill is a production cut; Plateveil remains the only OEM coating channel",
        },
        "executed_action": {
